# TA-IPMI — IPMI BMC Telemetry Add-on

Collects server BMC health via `ipmitool` (local open interface) on the Splunk host:
- Sensor readings (temperature, fan RPM, voltage, watts) + chassis/BMC status as JSON events to `index=main`, sourcetype `ipmi:status`
- Numeric sensors as time-series metrics to `index=metrics`, sourcetype `ipmi:metrics` (metric names `ipmi.*`)
- New System Event Log (SEL) records as events to `index=main`, sourcetype `ipmi:sel` (each record indexed exactly once)

Dashboards: **IPMI Overview** (chassis/BMC status, current sensor table, SEL log) and **IPMI Metrics** (trended temp/fan/voltage/power via mstats).

## Prerequisites

On every host where the inputs run:

1. **ipmitool must be installed** — this is the only external dependency:
   - Debian/Ubuntu: `apt-get install -y ipmitool`
   - RHEL/CentOS/Rocky/Alma: `yum install -y ipmitool` (or `dnf install -y ipmitool`)
   - SLES: `zypper install ipmitool`
2. **A server-class BMC the OS can reach via the system interface.** Kernel drivers loaded (typical on bare-metal servers):
   `modprobe ipmi_si ipmi_devintf` — this creates `/dev/ipmi0`.
   Check with: `ipmitool -I open mc info`
   On hosts without a local BMC (workstations, VMs, cloud), the inputs detect the missing
   `/dev/ipmi0`, log a short notice to `splunkd.log`, and exit cleanly; disable them there
   with an `local/inputs.conf` override (`disabled = 1`).
3. Splunk Enterprise 9.x (uses the built-in Python 3; inputs set `python.version = python3`).
4. An index named `metrics` with `datatype=metric` accessible for the metric stream
   (the app intentionally does **not** ship indexes.conf; it reuses your metrics index).
5. The splunk user must be able to execute `ipmitool -I open ...` (on some distros this needs
   the user in group `ipmi` or access to `/dev/ipmi0`).

## Install

Apps > Install app from file with `TA-IPMI.tar.gz`, or extract into `$SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/`.
Restart (or wait for auto-reload) and collection starts every 60s (SEL every 120s).

## Verify

    index=main sourcetype="ipmi:status" | head
    index=main sourcetype="ipmi:sel" | head
    index=metrics | mstats avg("ipmi.cpu_temp") span=1m

## Troubleshooting

- "Command `sdr list full` unsupported, trying plain" lines are normal (driver-dependent).
- No data: run `ipmitool -I open sdr list` as the splunk user. If that fails, the app will too.
- `Could not open device at /dev/ipmi0`: load `ipmi_si`/`ipmi_devintf` kernel modules or disable on BMC-less hosts.
- BAD_METRIC_EVENT: ensure props.conf `[ipmi:metrics]` TRANSFORMS/METRIC-SCHEMA and transforms.conf stanzas were not overridden in `local/`, and `index=metrics` is a metric index.
- SEL duplicates only appear if `$SPLUNK_HOME/var/lib/splunk/TA-IPMI/sel_last_id` is deleted (it is a high-water mark store).

